","code":"RS_ctrtot_net_exp","by_year":{"2017-18":67438.0,"2018-19":72427.0,"2019-20":74893.0,"2020-21":79671.0,"2021-22":82449.0,"2022-23":87660.0,"2023-24":95559.0,"2024-25":103014.0},"prov":{"description":"Financing - COUNCIL TAX REQUIREMENT (TOTAL OF LINES 805 TO 885)","form":"RS","row":"890","col":"1"}},{"label":"Net revenue expenditure","code":"RS_netrevexp_net_exp","by_year":{"2017-18":130831.0,"2018-19":130207.0,"2019-20":136128.0,"2020-21":125414.0,"2021-22":146102.0,"2022-23":133112.0,"2023-24":143197.0,"2024-25":174715.0},"prov":{"description":"NET current expenditure - NET REVENUE EXPENDITURE (TOTAL OF LINES 800 TO 804)","form":"RS","row":"805","col":"1"}}]}],"context":[{"label":"Resident population","value":213528,"year":"2020 est.","kind":"int"},{"label":"GVA (balanced, total)","value":6639000.0,"year":"2023","kind":"money"},{"label":"GVA per head","value":28737,"year":"2023","kind":"gbp"},{"label":"GDP per head","value":33128,"year":"2023","kind":"gbp"},{"label":"Band D council tax (area bill)","value":2439.93,"year":"2026-27","kind":"gbp"},{"label":"Band D \u2014 council's own element","value":2019.62,"year":"2026-27","kind":"gbp"}]}},"dossier":{"summary":null,"compliance":null,"documents":[],"read_documents":[],"calendar":null,"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Luton Council uses emergency reserves to balance budget as spending pressures mount","lead":"Luton Council's budget forecast for 2026/27 balances only after deploying \u00a31.764m of its contingency\u2014money set aside to cover unexpected costs\u2014to offset underlying spending pressures of \u00a32.533m. The council faces demand-led pressures across adult social care and schools special needs support. Adult social care forecasts a \u00a31.7m overspend despite additional government funding to address chronic underfunding, driven by demographic growth and rising care costs. The High Needs Block\u2014the part of school funding for children with special needs and disabilities\u2014forecasts a \u00a32.83m overspend after a surge in requests for assessments following national education reforms. Planned savings are slipping into the next financial year. The council is also reviewing its capital spending programme\u2014money for long-term assets like buildings and roads\u2014due to concerns about the cost of borrowing.","iso":"2026-09-17","paper_title":"9. Appendix A - 2026-27 Quarter 1 Budget Monitoring Exec Report","paper_url":"https://democracy.luton.gov.uk/CMIS5Public/Document.ashx?czJKcaeAi5tUFL1DTL2UE4zNRBcoShgo=gvEJauIclzjIRc3huMcaH4ui4MKbArm3lZiqD2D8WewcdkHIpfKkVQ%3d%3d&amp;rUzwRPf%2bZ3zd4E7Ikn8Lyw%3d%3d=pwRE6AGJFLDNlh225F5QMaQWCtPHwdhUfCZ%2fLUQzgA2uL5jNRG4jdQ%3d%3d&amp;mCTIbCubSFfXsDGW9IXnlg%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;kCx1AnS9%2fpWZQ40DXFvdEw%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;uJovDxwdjMPoYv%2bAJvYtyA%3d%3d=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;FgPlIEJYlotS%2bYGoBi5olA%3d%3d=NHdURQburHA%3d&amp;d9Qjj0ag1Pd993jsyOJqFvmyB7X0CSQK=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNR9xqBux0r1Q8Za60lavYmz=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNQ16B2MHuCpMRKZMwaG1PaO=ctNJFf55vVA%3d","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Luton set to receive \u00a36.2m for special needs school reform if government approves plan on 21 September","lead":"Luton council will receive \u00a32.2m in the first year to overhaul its special educational needs and disabilities (SEND) provision if the government approves its reform plan at a decision meeting on 21 September. The total funding, over three years, amounts to \u00a36.2m. The council has already committed \u00a32.2m in capital spending on two new special schools and inclusion bases by the end of this month. The reform centres on shifting how the council supports its 3,361 children with education, health and care plans (EHCPs), most of whom are currently in mainstream schools. The council has identified risks: demand for EHCPs could surge before new laws take effect, and if mainstream schools lack proper funding for inclusion support, rising exclusions could push costs up rather than down.","iso":"2026-09-16","paper_title":"SEND Reform Plan Update","paper_url":"https://democracy.luton.gov.uk/CMIS5Public/Document.ashx?czJKcaeAi5tUFL1DTL2UE4zNRBcoShgo=0RLy8t9VZPJCcEQNdzdZ0lUmVKvGRN7S%2fzKZP5JfWutD75TgAfI9bA%3d%3d&amp;rUzwRPf%2bZ3zd4E7Ikn8Lyw%3d%3d=pwRE6AGJFLDNlh225F5QMaQWCtPHwdhUfCZ%2fLUQzgA2uL5jNRG4jdQ%3d%3d&amp;mCTIbCubSFfXsDGW9IXnlg%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;kCx1AnS9%2fpWZQ40DXFvdEw%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;uJovDxwdjMPoYv%2bAJvYtyA%3d%3d=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;FgPlIEJYlotS%2bYGoBi5olA%3d%3d=NHdURQburHA%3d&amp;d9Qjj0ag1Pd993jsyOJqFvmyB7X0CSQK=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNR9xqBux0r1Q8Za60lavYmz=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNQ16B2MHuCpMRKZMwaG1PaO=ctNJFf55vVA%3d","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-10-01","committee":"01 October 2026","paper_title":"8 - Appendix 1 - Corporate Complaints Annual Performance Report (written) - 2026 v1.3","paper_url":"https://democracy.luton.gov.uk/CMIS5Public/Document.ashx?czJKcaeAi5tUFL1DTL2UE4zNRBcoShgo=E4QLQA9U%2bVHqiiw8wwdKjTHEO6%2f9GKEbiX9Ld1Xhnmz2fIOztDIZYg%3d%3d&amp;rUzwRPf%2bZ3zd4E7Ikn8Lyw%3d%3d=pwRE6AGJFLDNlh225F5QMaQWCtPHwdhUfCZ%2fLUQzgA2uL5jNRG4jdQ%3d%3d&amp;mCTIbCubSFfXsDGW9IXnlg%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;kCx1AnS9%2fpWZQ40DXFvdEw%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;uJovDxwdjMPoYv%2bAJvYtyA%3d%3d=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;FgPlIEJYlotS%2bYGoBi5olA%3d%3d=NHdURQburHA%3d&amp;d9Qjj0ag1Pd993jsyOJqFvmyB7X0CSQK=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNR9xqBux0r1Q8Za60lavYmz=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNQ16B2MHuCpMRKZMwaG1PaO=ctNJFf55vVA%3d","headline":"Council's actual complaints performance of 62.4% in-SLA falls 17.6 percentage points short of the new 80% corporate target.","detail":"Luton established an 80% in-SLA target 'for the first time' in the refreshed framework (effective January 2026). FY 2025/26 closed at 62.4% combined in-SLA (Stage 1: 62.6%, Stage 2: 61.4%). Performance did improve quarter-on-quarter from 60.8% (Q1) to 65.5% (Q4). The council projects reaching 80% in H2 FY 2026/27, conditional on achieving 100% training completion, Children's recovery plan delivery, and new platform implementation.","category":"governance","matters":"The council is publicly missing its own recently-established performance standard by a material margin. While quarterly improvement is evident, a 17.6 percentage point gap indicates capability or resource constraints in complaint handling that may reflect broader operational issues.","figures":"62.4% actual vs 80% target; 17.6 percentage point gap; quarterly progression 60.8% (Q1) to 65.5% (Q4)","quote":"It remains 17.6% below the new 80% corporate target","material":true},{"iso":"2026-10-01","committee":"01 October 2026","paper_title":"8 - Appendix 1 - Corporate Complaints Annual Performance Report (written) - 2026 v1.3","paper_url":"https://democracy.luton.gov.uk/CMIS5Public/Document.ashx?czJKcaeAi5tUFL1DTL2UE4zNRBcoShgo=E4QLQA9U%2bVHqiiw8wwdKjTHEO6%2f9GKEbiX9Ld1Xhnmz2fIOztDIZYg%3d%3d&amp;rUzwRPf%2bZ3zd4E7Ikn8Lyw%3d%3d=pwRE6AGJFLDNlh225F5QMaQWCtPHwdhUfCZ%2fLUQzgA2uL5jNRG4jdQ%3d%3d&amp;mCTIbCubSFfXsDGW9IXnlg%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;kCx1AnS9%2fpWZQ40DXFvdEw%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;uJovDxwdjMPoYv%2bAJvYtyA%3d%3d=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;FgPlIEJYlotS%2bYGoBi5olA%3d%3d=NHdURQburHA%3d&amp;d9Qjj0ag1Pd993jsyOJqFvmyB7X0CSQK=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNR9xqBux0r1Q8Za60lavYmz=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNQ16B2MHuCpMRKZMwaG1PaO=ctNJFf55vVA%3d","headline":"Housing Ombudsman issued one severe maladministration finding with 89% maladministration rate on housing determinations.","detail":"Six Housing Ombudsman determinations were issued in FY 2025/26: one severe maladministration, four standard maladministration findings, and one service failure, with one severe case now under senior oversight. Cases centred on 'repairs case-handling and clearer resident communication'. Total Housing Ombudsman compensation was \u00a32,600. All determinations were concentrated in Population Wellbeing, which holds the council's housing services.","category":"audit","matters":"Luton is a social housing landlord. A 89% maladministration rate and one severe finding indicate systemic issues in housing service delivery or complaint handling. Severe maladministration is a reputational and operational risk requiring sustained management attention.","figures":"6 determinations, 1 severe maladministration finding, 4 maladministration findings, 89% maladministration rate, \u00a32,600 compensation","quote":"One severe maladministration finding has been issued and is being managed through senior oversight. The maladministration rate of 89% remains high but is consistent with national landlord trends.","material":false},{"iso":"2026-10-01","committee":"01 October 2026","paper_title":"8 - Appendix 1 - Corporate Complaints Annual Performance Report (written) - 2026 v1.3","paper_url":"https://democracy.luton.gov.uk/CMIS5Public/Document.ashx?czJKcaeAi5tUFL1DTL2UE4zNRBcoShgo=E4QLQA9U%2bVHqiiw8wwdKjTHEO6%2f9GKEbiX9Ld1Xhnmz2fIOztDIZYg%3d%3d&amp;rUzwRPf%2bZ3zd4E7Ikn8Lyw%3d%3d=pwRE6AGJFLDNlh225F5QMaQWCtPHwdhUfCZ%2fLUQzgA2uL5jNRG4jdQ%3d%3d&amp;mCTIbCubSFfXsDGW9IXnlg%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;kCx1AnS9%2fpWZQ40DXFvdEw%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;uJovDxwdjMPoYv%2bAJvYtyA%3d%3d=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;FgPlIEJYlotS%2bYGoBi5olA%3d%3d=NHdURQburHA%3d&amp;d9Qjj0ag1Pd993jsyOJqFvmyB7X0CSQK=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNR9xqBux0r1Q8Za60lavYmz=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNQ16B2MHuCpMRKZMwaG1PaO=ctNJFf55vVA%3d","headline":"Ombudsman compensation claims fell 69% to \u00a34,750 from \u00a315,335, with LGSCO referrals declining from 64 to 41.","detail":"Total compensation ordered across LGSCO and Housing Ombudsman dropped from \u00a315,335 (FY 2024/25) to \u00a34,750 (FY 2025/26). LGSCO referrals fell from 64 to 41 year-on-year. The report notes this 'indicates a reduction in the severity or duration of upheld service failure'. 100% compliance with all LGSCO recommendations was maintained across all three years.","category":"audit","matters":"Ombudsman compensation represents direct financial exposure from service failures. A 69% reduction in compensation and falling referral volumes signal either fewer service failures or better early resolution, reducing unquantified future liability.","figures":"\u00a34,750 compensation (from \u00a315,335), -69%; LGSCO referrals 41 (from 64)","quote":"Combined financial remedy fell from \u00a315,335 to \u00a34,750","material":false},{"iso":"2026-10-01","committee":"01 October 2026","paper_title":"8 - Appendix 1 - Corporate Complaints Annual Performance Report (written) - 2026 v1.3","paper_url":"https://democracy.luton.gov.uk/CMIS5Public/Document.ashx?czJKcaeAi5tUFL1DTL2UE4zNRBcoShgo=E4QLQA9U%2bVHqiiw8wwdKjTHEO6%2f9GKEbiX9Ld1Xhnmz2fIOztDIZYg%3d%3d&amp;rUzwRPf%2bZ3zd4E7Ikn8Lyw%3d%3d=pwRE6AGJFLDNlh225F5QMaQWCtPHwdhUfCZ%2fLUQzgA2uL5jNRG4jdQ%3d%3d&amp;mCTIbCubSFfXsDGW9IXnlg%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;kCx1AnS9%2fpWZQ40DXFvdEw%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;uJovDxwdjMPoYv%2bAJvYtyA%3d%3d=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;FgPlIEJYlotS%2bYGoBi5olA%3d%3d=NHdURQburHA%3d&amp;d9Qjj0ag1Pd993jsyOJqFvmyB7X0CSQK=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNR9xqBux0r1Q8Za60lavYmz=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNQ16B2MHuCpMRKZMwaG1PaO=ctNJFf55vVA%3d","headline":"Children, Family & Education complaint volume surged 54% to 216, the sharpest rise across the council, in an already high-risk service performing at 34.3% in-SLA.","detail":"Complaints in Children, Family & Education rose from 140 to 216. Performance remained flat at 34.3% in-SLA despite this large increase, meaning complaint resolution is not keeping pace with rising demand. The report attributes this to 'statutory complexity in children's social care and SEND, and sustained capacity pressure' and flags the directorate as highest-risk, requiring a dedicated recovery plan with weekly leadership review, named SLT sponsor, and targets of 60% SLA by Q2 and 75% by year-end FY 2026/27.","category":"demand","matters":"A 54% volume surge in a statutory service that is already performing below 35% against an 80% target indicates service stress or capacity shortfall. This signals potential strain on the council's ability to deliver statutory children's services and manage associated costs and liability risk.","figures":"216 complaints (from 140), +54%, 34.3% in-SLA (vs 80% target), 52.9 average response days","quote":"Children, Family & Education is the highest-risk area (34.3%) with the sharpest volume rise (+54%)","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-17","committee":"17 September 2026","paper_title":"9. Appendix 1 - Detailed 2026-27 Quarter 1 Budget Monitoring Report","paper_url":"https://democracy.luton.gov.uk/CMIS5Public/Document.ashx?czJKcaeAi5tUFL1DTL2UE4zNRBcoShgo=EpQsHMzHf%2bYqBlqXfyMeSQVT%2fNk%2bowW8rogg6Yo4EegY%2fN6EJFx22g%3d%3d&amp;rUzwRPf%2bZ3zd4E7Ikn8Lyw%3d%3d=pwRE6AGJFLDNlh225F5QMaQWCtPHwdhUfCZ%2fLUQzgA2uL5jNRG4jdQ%3d%3d&amp;mCTIbCubSFfXsDGW9IXnlg%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;kCx1AnS9%2fpWZQ40DXFvdEw%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;uJovDxwdjMPoYv%2bAJvYtyA%3d%3d=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;FgPlIEJYlotS%2bYGoBi5olA%3d%3d=NHdURQburHA%3d&amp;d9Qjj0ag1Pd993jsyOJqFvmyB7X0CSQK=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNR9xqBux0r1Q8Za60lavYmz=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNQ16B2MHuCpMRKZMwaG1PaO=ctNJFf55vVA%3d","headline":"Investment property portfolio under pressure from voids and legal disputes; \u00a30.790m overspend forecast.","detail":"The council's Investment Properties forecast a \u00a30.790m overspend comprising \u00a30.516m income shortfall from vacant units (portfolio has voids affecting returns), \u00a30.2m income shortfall at Arndale Indoor Market due to 'an ongoing legal dispute with the operator,' and \u00a30.074m operational cost pressures. The council is undertaking a 'detailed assessment' but issues persist.","category":"income","matters":"Commercial property income is often used to support the general fund. Voids reduce that income and affect revenue resilience. A legal dispute with a tenant also represents a contingent liability exposure.","figures":"\u00a30.790m overspend; \u00a30.516m from vacant units; \u00a30.2m income shortfall at Arndale Indoor Market due to legal dispute","quote":"Investment Properties are forecasting a \u00a30.790m overspend, comprising a \u00a30.516m income shortfall from vacant units and properties, a \u00a30.2m service charge income shortfall at Arndale Indoor Market due to an ongoing legal dispute with the operator, and \u00a30.074m of operational cost pressures.","material":false}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-17"},"name":"Luton UA","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-25","since_iso":"2026-08-26","distress":false,"headline":"Investment property portfolio under pressure from voids and legal disputes; \u00a30.790m overspend forecast.","lead":"Commercial property income is often used to support the general fund. Voids reduce that income and affect revenue resilience. A legal dispute with a tenant also represents a contingent liability exposure.","also":["33 other findings in this window"],"watch":null,"n_findings":34,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"9. Appendix 1 - Detailed 2026-27 Quarter 1 Budget Monitoring Report","top_paper_url":"https://democracy.luton.gov.uk/CMIS5Public/Document.ashx?czJKcaeAi5tUFL1DTL2UE4zNRBcoShgo=EpQsHMzHf%2bYqBlqXfyMeSQVT%2fNk%2bowW8rogg6Yo4EegY%2fN6EJFx22g%3d%3d&amp;rUzwRPf%2bZ3zd4E7Ikn8Lyw%3d%3d=pwRE6AGJFLDNlh225F5QMaQWCtPHwdhUfCZ%2fLUQzgA2uL5jNRG4jdQ%3d%3d&amp;mCTIbCubSFfXsDGW9IXnlg%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;kCx1AnS9%2fpWZQ40DXFvdEw%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;uJovDxwdjMPoYv%2bAJvYtyA%3d%3d=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;FgPlIEJYlotS%2bYGoBi5olA%3d%3d=NHdURQburHA%3d&amp;d9Qjj0ag1Pd993jsyOJqFvmyB7X0CSQK=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNR9xqBux0r1Q8Za60lavYmz=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNQ16B2MHuCpMRKZMwaG1PaO=ctNJFf55vVA%3d","draft":true},"findings_total":124,"news_drafts_total":2}}